      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Little foxes have plotted inside the lion's cave! Straws have played at the sword-point. Though they knew who Gopativarman was, those wicked, unjust wretches committed this outrage in his own palace. Durjaya, let the search for those traitors proceed relentlessly. Proclaim it throughout the land with drumbeat. Hack that adulteress into pieces and show her before my eyes. Wash away the stain that has fallen on Kurinji country with the blood of those wastrels. Whoever has hidden those great sinners—whoever they may be—death penalty! Torture! Hmm, let it be done.",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The violent images and insults are translated as source rhetoric rather than softened. `பறை சாட்டுங்கள்` is rendered as public proclamation by drumbeat; `விபசாரி` is translated contextually as `adulteress`."
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
